\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Frequency dependence of the WSPR storm response. Spot reduction for the three HF bands during $Kp \ge 5$ storms. The 15\,m band shows substantially stronger suppression ($\SI {-38.7}{\percent }$) than 20\,m ($\SI {-27.7}{\percent }$) and 40\,m ($\SI {-27.2}{\percent }$), consistent with the dual-mechanism interpretation (MUF reduction on 15\,m, D-layer absorption on 20\,m/40\,m).}}{9}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:freq}{{3}{9}{Frequency dependence of the WSPR storm response. Spot reduction for the three HF bands during $Kp \ge 5$ storms. The 15\,m band shows substantially stronger suppression ($\SI {-38.7}{\percent }$) than 20\,m ($\SI {-27.7}{\percent }$) and 40\,m ($\SI {-27.2}{\percent }$), consistent with the dual-mechanism interpretation (MUF reduction on 15\,m, D-layer absorption on 20\,m/40\,m)}{figure.caption.8}{}}
